body: "# ADR-007 — S7 Projection Verify: ESAA + Hash Verification\n\n> **Status**: ACTIVE | **Date**: 2026-05-09 | **Author**: TACO Wave S7\n> **Deprecates**: N/A | **Supersedes**: N/A\n\n## Context\n\n`taco-forge plan --projection-verify` needs a deterministic hash of the activity\nhistory for a task, stored in the plan checkpoint and re-verified on subsequent\nruns. The hash must be stable across Python processes and independent of\nruntime-specific metadata.\n\n## Decision\n\nImplemented ESAA (Event Sourcing Algebraic Algorithm) in `plan_quality/projection.py`.\n\n### ESAA Canonical Form\n\n```\nkey1:value1,key2:value2,...   (sorted alphabetically, no trailing comma)\n```\n\n| Rule | Detail |\n|------|--------|\n| Keys sorted | alphabetically, ascending |\n| Scalar values | `str.strip()`, JSON-like for `int/float/bool/None` |\n| Nested dict | recursively canonicalized |\n| List values | `json.dumps(val, sort_keys=True)` |\n| **Exclude** | `meta.run` (runtime-derived, non-deterministic) |\n| Record separator | `\\n` between events |\n| Output terminator | trailing `\\n` after last record |\n\n### Hash Computation\n\n```\ncanonical_bytes = \"\\n\".join(canonical_parts) + \"\\n\"\nsha256 = SHA-256(canonical_bytes).hexdigest()\n```\n\n### Fallback Chain\n\n1. CLI: `touring activity replay --task-id <id> --json` (subprocess, 15s timeout)\n2. Direct scan: `activity.jsonl` parsed line-by-line; `JSONDecodeError` lines skipped\n\n### Exit Codes\n\n| Code | Meaning | Trigger |\n|------|---------|---------|\n| 0 | OK | `got == expected` |\n| 5 | MISMATCH | `got != expected` |\n| 6 | CORRUPTED | Exception during `replay_projection()` |\n\n### Data Structures\n\n- VerifyOutcome: OK / MISMATCH / CORRUPTED\n- ProjectedState: task_id, canonical_bytes, sha256, event_count, projected_at\n- VerifyResult: outcome, expected_hash, got_hash, task_id, event_count, detail\n\n### CLI Integration\n\n```bash\ntaco-forge plan --projection-verify \\\n    --task-id <id> \\\n    --expected-projection-hash <sha256> \\\n    [--activity-path <path>]\n```\n\nOutput (stdout, JSON):\n```json\n{\n  \"verify_status\": \"ok\",\n  \"task_id\": \"...\",\n  \"event_count\": 3,\n  \"projection_sha256\": \"...\"\n}\n```\n\n### Files\n\n| File | LOC | Purpose |\n|------|-----|---------|\n| `lib/plan_quality/projection.py` | ~298 | Core ESAA module |\n| `lib/plan_quality/cli.py` | +50 | Stage 5/7 wiring in `generate` |\n| `tests/plan_quality/test_plan_projection.py` | ~210 | 20 unit tests |\n| `tests/e2e/projection_verify_e2e.py` | ~170 | 6 E2E tests |\n\n### Test Coverage\n\n| ID | Description |\n|----|-------------|\n| T7.1 | empty store → known constant hash |\n| T7.2 | canonicalize single event |\n| T7.3 | canonicalize excludes `meta.run` |\n| T7.4 | verify ok (matching hash) |\n| T7.5 | verify mismatch |\n| T7.6 | verify corrupted (malformed JSONL) |\n| T7.7 | full plan flow exits 0 on clean |\n| T7.8 | re-emit determinism (same hash twice) |\n| T7.9 | mismatched hash exits 5 |\n| T7.10 | corrupted events exits 6 |\n| T7.11 | empty activity → 64-char SHA-256 |\n| T7.12 | JSON output format |\n\n## Consequences\n\n- Hash is deterministic regardless of Python process ID or timestamp\n- `meta.run` exclusion prevents replay divergence from runtime metadata\n- Fallback scan handles environments where `touring` CLI is unavailable\n- Exit codes 0/5/6 are conventional Unix (match/mismatch/error)\n\n## Lessons\n\n1. `datetime.isoformat()` takes no `timestamp` kwarg\n2. subprocess module has no `.os` attribute — use top-level `import os`\n3. Malformed JSONL in fallback scan should be **skipped**, not raise CORRUPTED\n4. Bash string quoting in heredocs is fragile — prefer Python E2E driver\n"
